# LAN / direct-connect game setup on the procedural UI system. Units: 1 = frame height / 1080. The same frame as the
# skirmish setup: title top-left, the players table (shared block) on the left with the lobby chat under it, the map and
# rules panels (shared blocks) on the right, Back and Start in the bottom bar. Every row carries the player's accept
# marker (ButtonAcceptN, the stock image) at its left edge, so the slot column starts at 116.

# the root draws the blueprint frame; GadgetParent holds the controls (made frame-sized, draws nothing); LINE is the old rule
hide $LanGameOptionsMenuParent
window $GadgetParent left top 0 0 1920 1080
hide $GadgetParent
hide $LINE

window $StaticTextTitle left top 64 40 560 48 title
ruler left top 64 94 560

include GameSetupPlayers.layout

# accept markers and the narrower slot combos
window $ButtonAccept0 left top 84 214 20 20
window $ButtonAccept1 left top 84 262 20 20
window $ButtonAccept2 left top 84 310 20 20
window $ButtonAccept3 left top 84 358 20 20
window $ButtonAccept4 left top 84 406 20 20
window $ButtonAccept5 left top 84 454 20 20
window $ButtonAccept6 left top 84 502 20 20
window $ButtonAccept7 left top 84 550 20 20
window $ComboBoxPlayer0 left top 116 204 228 40 dropdown
window $ComboBoxPlayer1 left top 116 252 228 40 dropdown
window $ComboBoxPlayer2 left top 116 300 228 40 dropdown
window $ComboBoxPlayer3 left top 116 348 228 40 dropdown
window $ComboBoxPlayer4 left top 116 396 228 40 dropdown
window $ComboBoxPlayer5 left top 116 444 228 40 dropdown
window $ComboBoxPlayer6 left top 116 492 228 40 dropdown
window $ComboBoxPlayer7 left top 116 540 228 40 dropdown

# lobby chat under the table
rule left top 84 600 1064
window $ListboxChatWindowLanGame left top 84 612 1064 268 list
window $TextEntryChat left top 84 896 1004 40 entry
window $ButtonEmote left top 1096 896 52 40

include GameSetupMap.layout
include GameSetupRules.layout

window $ButtonBack left bottom 64 40 180 44 button
window $ButtonStart right bottom 64 40 220 44 primary
